# Supabase RLS & multi-tenancy — production contract

The tenant is `organizations.id`. Every persisted row carries
`organization_id`. There is no “default workspace”. The Stripe customer is
**per organization**, never per user.

## Clients

| Module | Key | RLS | Who may import |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `lib/supabase/client.ts` | anon / publishable | on | Client Components only |
| `lib/supabase/server.ts` | anon + cookies | on | Server Components, Route Handlers, `requireUser` |
| `lib/supabase/admin.ts` | **service_role** | bypass | After an independent trust check (verified Stripe/Lemon HMAC, cron secret). `import "server-only"`. |
| `lib/supabase/proxy.ts` | anon + request cookies | on | `proxy.ts` only |

Never put `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in a Client Component or
`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variable.

## Identity

- Server identity = `supabase.auth.getClaims()`, then
  `readSubjectFromClaims` → `loadTenantUser`.
- `getSession()` is not proof of identity (can be stale / spoofable on the
  server).
- `loadTenantUser` parses PostgREST embeds with Zod row schemas
  (`lib/supabase/row-schemas.ts`). Do not `as UserJoinRow`.
- Inactive members (`is_active = false`) are not `isUsableTenantUser`.

## SQL / RLS

- New tables: numbered migration under `supabase/migrations/`,
  `enable row level security` **and** `force row level security`.
- Default deny. Grant `authenticated` only the verbs they need.
  Billing writes (`subscriptions`, `stripe_webhook_events`) stay
  service-role only.
- Policies must compare `organization_id` to
  `public.user_organization_id()` (SECURITY DEFINER helper). Do not read
  `organization_id` from the client body to *join* a tenant.
- Invites require a verified token. Signup trigger
  `handle_new_user()` always creates a **new** org as `owner`. Forged
  `organization_id` in user metadata must be ignored.
- Roles: `owner | admin | member | billing | viewer`. Enforce in RLS
  (`user_has_role`) **and** in server code (`hasRole`,
  `decidePortalAccess`).

## Queries

- Every `.from("…")` in user-scoped code relies on RLS. Still pass
  `.eq("organization_id", orgId)` when the query is not already implied,
  so a missing policy fails closed in review.
- Select lists should be explicit when joining (`profiles (*)`,
  `organizations (*)`).
- Do not log access tokens, service-role keys, or full JWT payloads.
